✅ **Early bug detection** - Catches structural changes
✅ **Type safety** - Validates data types
✅ **Documentation** - Schema serves as living documentation
✅ **Client confidence** - Clients know what to expect

**Basic JSON Schema Example**:

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["id", "name", "email"],
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "maxLength": 100
    },
    "email": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "email"
    },
    "age": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0,
      "maximum": 150
    },
    "createdAt": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

