**Key Insight**: E2E integration tests provide the highest confidence but are expensive. Focus on critical business workflows that span multiple services.

Effective integration testing requires careful planning and the right strategies. Here are proven patterns and best practices for testing integrations between services, databases, and external systems.

**Integration Testing Best Practices**:

| Practice | Description | Implementation |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| **Test Isolation** | Each test runs independently | Transactions, test containers, database per test |
| **Realistic Data** | Use production-like data | Fixtures, factories, data generators |
| **Idempotent Tests** | Tests can run multiple times | Unique data per run, UUIDs, timestamps |
| **Fast Feedback** | Optimize for speed | Parallel execution, selective testing, caching |
| **Resilience Testing** | Test failure modes | Chaos engineering, timeouts, circuit breakers |
| **Contract Testing** | Verify service agreements | Pact, OpenAPI validation, consumer-driven contracts |

