Stress testing pushes your API beyond normal limits to find its breaking point. It answers: "How much load can it handle before failing, and how does it fail?"

**Stress Testing Goals**:

✅ Find maximum capacity before failure
✅ Understand failure modes (graceful degradation vs crash)
✅ Identify bottlenecks under extreme load
✅ Test auto-scaling triggers
✅ Plan capacity and headroom
✅ Prepare for traffic spikes

**K6 Stress Test Example**:

```javascript
// stress-test.js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
