**Scalability Testing Best Practices**:

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Test Both Directions** | Scale up AND down | Add scale-down in tests |
| **Measure Efficiency** | Cost per request | Track resource usage |
| **Find Bottlenecks** | Database, network, CPU | Profile under load |
| **Test Auto-scaling** | Verify triggers | Monitor instance count |
| **Plan for Headroom** | Don't run at 100% | Leave 30% buffer |
| **Document Limits** | Know your max | Track breaking points |

**Key Insight**: Scalability isn't just about handling more load—it's about doing it efficiently. Linear scaling at 2x cost for 2x load is good; 3x cost for 2x load is not.

