**CI/CD Performance Testing Best Practices**:

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Fast Feedback** | Developers need quick results | Run smoke perf tests on PR |
| **Baseline Comparison** | Detect regressions | Store historical results |
| **Fail Gracefully** | Don't block all PRs | Allow overrides with justification |
| **Test in Staging** | Don't impact production | Use staging environment |
| **Monitor Trends** | Gradual degradation | Dashboard with trends |
| **Alert on Regressions** | Catch early | Email/Slack notifications |

**Key Insight**: Performance testing in CI/CD shifts left, catching issues when they're cheapest to fix. The goal is to make performance a first-class citizen in your development workflow.

A comprehensive performance testing strategy combines all test types into a coherent program that ensures your API is fast, stable, and scalable.

**Performance Testing Matrix**:

| Test Type | Frequency | Duration | Environment | Goals |
|-----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-------|
| **Baseline** | Every PR | 1 min | Dev/CI | Quick regression check |
| **Load Test** | Daily | 10 min | Staging | Verify under expected load |
| **Stress Test** | Weekly | 30 min | Staging | Find breaking points |
| **Spike Test** | Weekly | 15 min | Staging | Test surge handling |
| **Soak Test** | Monthly | 24 hours | Staging | Detect leaks/degradation |
| **Scalability** | Quarterly | 2 hours | Staging+Prod | Plan capacity |

