**Key Insight:** Data integrity is the foundation of a trustworthy API. Test it thoroughly and continuously.

Race conditions occur when multiple requests access shared data concurrently, and the final outcome depends on the timing or interleaving of operations. They're among the most subtle and dangerous bugs in APIs.

**Common Concurrency Problems:**

| Problem | Description | Example |
|---------|-------------|---------|
| **Race Condition** | Outcome depends on timing | Two users buying last item |
| **Deadlock** | Requests waiting for each other | Transaction A locks X, waits for Y; B locks Y, waits for X |
| **Starvation** | Request never gets resources | Low-priority requests always skipped |
| **Lost Update** | One write overwrites another | Two users edit same profile simultaneously |
| **Dirty Read** | Reading uncommitted data | Reading balance during transfer |
| **Non-repeatable Read** | Same query returns different values | Read during update |

**The Classic Race Condition:**

```javascript
// Vulnerable code
async function buyLastItem(userId, itemId) {
  const item = await db.items.findById(itemId);

  if (item.stock > 0) {
    // Race window starts here
    item.stock -= 1;
    await db.orders.create({ userId, itemId });
    await item.save();
    // Race window ends here
    return { success: true };
  }

  return { success: false, error: 'Out of stock' };
}

// Two users simultaneously execute this
// Both see stock = 1, both decrement to 0
// Result: oversold by 1 item
```

**Key Insight:** Race conditions are hard to reproduce but devastating when they happen. Systematic testing is the only way to catch them.

The foundation of concurrency testing is sending multiple requests simultaneously to trigger race conditions.

**Basic Parallel Request Test:**

```javascript
// concurrency/parallel-test.js
const axios = require('axios');

class ParallelRequestTester {
  constructor(baseURL) {
    this.baseURL = baseURL;
    this.results = [];
  }

  async sendParallel(endpoint, method, data, count = 10) {
    const requests = [];

    for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
      requests.push(
        axios({
          method,
          url: `${this.baseURL}${endpoint}`,
          data,
          validateStatus: () => true // Accept any status
        })
      );
    }

    const responses = await Promise.all(requests);
    this.results = responses.map((r, i) => ({
      requestId: i,
      status: r.status,
      data: r.data
    }));

    return this.results;
  }

  analyze() {
    const successCount = this.results.filter(r => r.status === 200).length;
    const errorCount = this.results.filter(r => r.status >= 400).length;

    // Look for anomalies
    const unexpectedSuccess = successCount > 1; // If only one should succeed
    const inconsistentData = this.checkDataConsistency();

    return {
      total: this.results.length,
      success: successCount,
      errors: errorCount,
      unexpectedSuccess,
      inconsistentData,
      details: this.results
    };
  }

  checkDataConsistency() {
    // Check if responses contain conflicting data
    const successfulResponses = this.results.filter(r => r.status === 200);
    if (successfulResponses.length <= 1) return false;

    // Compare data from successful responses
    const first = successfulResponses[0].data;
    return successfulResponses.some(r => 
      JSON.stringify(r.data) !== JSON.stringify(first)
    );
  }
}

// Usage
describe('Parallel Request Tests', () => {
  it('should handle parallel purchases correctly', async () => {
    const tester = new ParallelRequestTester('https://api.example.com');

    // Reset stock to 1
    await axios.post('https://api.example.com/test/reset-stock', { itemId: 123, stock: 1 });

    // Send 5 parallel purchase requests
    const results = await tester.sendParallel('/items/123/buy', 'POST', {}, 5);
    const analysis = tester.analyze();

    // Only one should succeed
    expect(analysis.success).toBe(1);
    expect(analysis.errors).toBe(4);

    // Verify final stock is 0
    const stock = await axios.get('https://api.example.com/items/123');
    expect(stock.data.stock).toBe(0);
  });
});
```

